   what the legacy `/F` of the Unicode name holds: b'\xfcber-\x0c\x80.bin'. 𓂀 has no
   PDFDocEncoding byte, so pdf-lib writes `\x0c\x80` there and the UTF-16BE `/UF`
   beside it carries the real name — which is what pypdf lists above, while poppler
   prints `/F` and shows the substitution. Record, not fixed here: the bytes a user
   downloads come from `/UF`, and every reader above extracted them intact.

